xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:158:### 2.1 Lemma classification: td-agnostic as proved versus td-7 data
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:164:| item | td-agnostic kernel already proved | td-7-specific part that does not port |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:165:|---|---|---|
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:166:| **L-A** | On any merge-free `M=1` branch, `l=1`; charged directions are shape-impossible and `M=1` propagates, budget-independently. | “Frozen at `(w,M)=(2,1)`,” absence of clean state-changing resonances, degree-2 anchor, and the `n=1` X-gap.  L-A proves uncharged, not constant `w`. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:167:| **AM** | `M=1` is absorbing on a merge-free chain. | The first charged menu `{(21,15),(20,16)}`, `lambda=2`, `i=2`, and pruning of other steps use seed `(3/2,2)` and a single class-C target.  An `M=1` branch may legally enter a higher mixed/nested merge. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:168:| **WIN** | Degree-growth and ratio estimates are reusable techniques. | The lemma uses pole top `5/2`, degrees `2/4`, budget 5, the 69-state closure, and competing maximum `2/5`.  It is not a td-uniform theorem. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:169:| **TERM** | The strategy “bound every rootward gap below X” is reusable. | The proof uses the 16 td-7 cells and `deg p_{f,G}>=42`; an inner merge plus later sibling is not a td-7 terminal. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:170:| **tower-N1** | A state-preserving zero-cost insertion has `n=1`, clean form `(l*nu,nu+1)`, and the gcd identity. | It does not classify state-changing clean resonances or eligible states. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:171:| **tower-N2** | Only `gcd(l*nu,nu+1)=gcd(l,nu+1)` is generic. | Odd `nu`/odd `P_pre` uses the td-7 pre-charge state `M=2`.  States `M=3,5` require new congruence classes. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:172:| **tower-N3** | Simultaneously alive vertices impose the intersection of their exponent caps. | `k|2` uses pole exponent 4, first-charge exponent `2P_pre`, and N2 oddness.  The new cap is entry/state dependent, typically `k | gcd(pdeg_P,i_first*P_pre)`. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:173:| **tower-N4** | A neutral inserted above full degree `Dprev` has gap `(nu+1)/(Dprev*nu)`, independent of `l`; if `Dprev>=4`, it is `<=3/8`. | Its comparison with an X-gap `>1/2`, and shrinkage of the A/C gaps, are td-7 numerical inputs. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:174:| **E5F** | Under resolved Q+E5, `n=nu_U*kbar_G-nu_G*kbar_U>=1`; the intermediate `rho` identity is general. | `X=kbar-2`, minimal-pad `n=-2`, and the filed `n=-1` family are td-7 frame corollaries. |
xmodel/sol-td11-13-scope.md:175:| **A/B/C exhaustion** | The displayed divisibility calculations are identities once the td-7 packet is assumed. | The packet is `(k0,l0)=(2,3)`, `alpha1=3/2`, cap `k|2`, X-gap `(nu+1)/(2nu)`, empty top `5/2` window, and prefix menu `{1,3/2,2}`.  Type `(2,5)`, type `(3,4)`, resonant X, or another cap needs a new exhaustion. |
