TOWER-TD11.md:1:# TOWER-TD11.md — entry-level clash analysis for the three td-11 entries
TOWER-TD11.md:53:## 0. The letter-domain law (used everywhere below)
TOWER-TD11.md:69:## 1. Entry 11-A — `(2,3): [1@2;2] + [2@3;4]`, pole top `5/2`
TOWER-TD11.md:71:| item | value (exact) |
TOWER-TD11.md:72:|---|---|
TOWER-TD11.md:73:| chain-1 freeze | seed `(2,1)`: L-A hypotheses HOLD (merge-free `M=1`; `w=2` has no state-changing clean resonance, scope:278) — **frozen**, td-7-style |
TOWER-TD11.md:74:| `gap(X)` | `(nu_X+1)/(2 nu_X) ∈ (1/2, 2/3]`, `nu_X` odd (domain law `a = 2`) |
TOWER-TD11.md:75:| chain-2 menu | charged `{7/16, 2/5, 3/8, 5/14, 11/32}`; pure `<= 3/11`; neutral `<= 3/8`; resonance `5/8` |
TOWER-TD11.md:76:| non-resonant window content | NONE: every non-resonant gap `< 1/2 < gap(X)` |
TOWER-TD11.md:77:| **the intruder** | the zero-cost clean resonance `Delta=3, n=2, nu=2`: `w: 3→2`, `M: 2→1`, `pdeg = 8`, `dq = 5`, **`gap = 5/8`, `lambda = 0`**. In-window iff `5/8 > gap(X)` iff `nu_X > 4`, i.e. odd `nu_X >= 5`; `nu_X = 3` clears it (`2/3 > 5/8`). Padded copies `5/(8A) < 1/2` are below every X |
TOWER-TD11.md:78:| **the intruder's kill (μ-robust)** | the resonance is an **M-drop** (`2 → 1`), so `μ | M = 1` forces `μ = 1` on that branch — the `μ = M` escape of grok-nfd finding 1 is CLOSED by the drop (NF-D D5: drops are irreversible). The scale is then compared raw: `v_2(8·A·B) >= 3` for every `w=3` prefix `A` and `w=2` suffix `B`, vs chain-1's `v_2(2·Pi) = 1` for every odd stack — `H8_EQUAL_QUOTIENT_VP_MISMATCH` fires on EVERY route shape (gate A4; the promoted 11-A row, now μ-checked) |
TOWER-TD11.md:79:| Case-A refusal | `k = 2 nu_X` (odd `nu_X >= 3`) divides neither cap candidate `2` nor `4` — robust under the unresolved cap (see OB-5: `w=3` `P_pre` parity is unforced, so the td-7 `k|2` derivation does not port verbatim; `k|4` is the conservative joint cap and refuses Case A equally) |
TOWER-TD11.md:80:| synchronized window | INHABITED under `μ = (1,2)`: `2Pi_1 = 4Pi_2/2 ⇒ Pi_1 = Pi_2` (NF-D round 2) — the clash is about real routes |
TOWER-TD11.md:81:| **verdict** | **WINDOW CLEAN-CONDITIONAL**: non-resonant routes → empty prefix → Case-A refusal; resonant routes → H8-dead. Conditional on the promoted H8 row and on route realization (OB-4/OB-10) |
TOWER-TD11.md:91:## 2. Entry 11-B — `(2,5): [1@3;2] + [3@4/3;6]`, pole top `7/2`
TOWER-TD11.md:93:| item | value (exact) |
TOWER-TD11.md:94:|---|---|
TOWER-TD11.md:95:| chain-1 freeze | seed `(1@3;2)`: **NOT td-7-frozen.** L-A still gives uncharged + `M=1` propagation (its kernel is budget- and `w`-independent), but `w = 3` carries one classified state-changing clean resonance: `(n,nu) = (2,2)`, `gap 5/4`, `w: 3→2` (scope:281-283). Freeze holds MODULO that step |
TOWER-TD11.md:96:| `gap(X)`, neutral | `(nu_X+1)/(2 nu_X)` over `3 ∤ nu_X` (parity free, `nu_X = 2` legal): `∈ (1/2, 3/4]`, max `3/4` at `nu_X = 2` |
TOWER-TD11.md:97:| `gap(X)`, resonant | pole-adjacent resonance: `X = 5/4`; padded copies `5/(4 Pi) <= 5/8 < 3/4` lie BELOW the pole-adjacent X (scope:357-360) |
TOWER-TD11.md:98:| chain-2 menu | charged `{5/22, 3/14, 7/34}`; pure `{1/5, 2/11}`; neutral `<= 1/5`; NO resonance. Max `5/22` |
TOWER-TD11.md:99:| window | **EMPTY at one step**: `5/22 < 1/2 <` every X (neutral or resonant); the resonant X `5/4` also has an empty window above it (all pads `<= 3/4`, opponent `<= 5/22`) |
TOWER-TD11.md:100:| Case-A refusal | `k = 2 nu_X` divides neither cap candidate `2` nor `6`, for EVERY legal `nu_X` — including even `nu_X = 2` (`k = 4`). **Load-bearing near-miss (gate X4): `nu_X = 3` WOULD give `k = 6 | 6` — a Case-A escape — and is excluded exactly by the domain law `3 ∤ nu` at `w = 3`.** The clash uses the letter domain, not just the gap order |
