xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:4308:SHEET6-DEPTH.md-60-is a maximal run F_0 → F_1 → … → F_d of the characteristic sequence
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:4337:SHEET6-MULTIPOLE.md-87-Poles have m_F = 0 (Prop 5.1(i) + Not 5.1/5.2), so the h-family is {g} (Prop 4.2) and M_{P_i} = gcd(deg p_{P_i}, deg p_{g,P_i}) (Not 8.1). St 5.2(i): deg p/deg p_g = α/β at poles, so (deg p, deg p_g) = b_i(α,β) and M_{P_i} = b_i·gcd(α,β) = b_i = deg p_{P_i}/α. (Check: reproduces all 11 rows of table (23), p. 46, and St 9.6's printed M = 2 = gcd(4,6).) β-minimal: Λ(P) = a b αβ/ν (Prop 5.6 (19)) = β forces ν = abα; St 5.2(ii): ν | α ⇒ ab = 1 ⇒ b = 1; ν | β ⇒ abα | β with gcd(α,β) = 1 ⇒ α = 1, contra St 2.1. Prime Λ: case ν | α: Λ = ab(α/ν)β divisible by β ≥ 3, so Λ = β and a = b = α/ν = 1; case ν | β: Λ = abα(β/ν) divisible by α ≥ 2, so Λ = α < β ≤ Λ (Prop 5.7) — empty. Since the type (α,β) is global (Lemma 2.1), this is per-vertex, valid at every td — repairing the Λ = td-dependence of SHEET6-TDUNIFORM §2. ∎
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:4343:SHEET6-MULTIPOLE.md:93:Merge ≠ pole: an arriving direction has full multiplicity deg p_{H_e} ≥ 2, contradicting Prop 5.3(v) squarefreeness. Let some μ_j = 1. (a) k = 0: exactly the D5(c) manufacture, now read at G — every root of p_G supports, via Prop 6.8's same-branch pole, an incoming chain of one of the m poles; the roots of p_G are precisely the r arriving directions, in distinct ν-orbits (St 3.18: one continuation per orbit). (b) Equal-quotient: deg p_{H_e} = mult(p_G^{full}, c_e) = i·μ_e (St 3.17(i) + Prop 8.1(i): p^{full} = ⊖p^i); with μ_j = 1, i = deg p_{H_j} ≥ 2. (c) q-shape by root/eta laws [P2] as in D5(d). (d) Arithmetic: dq = (r+l)ν + 1 ≡ 1 (mod ν) forces gcd(M_G, ν) = 1 (Prop 8.1(v): M_G = gcd(dp, dq)); with dp = (Σμ_e)ν, any common divisor is coprime to ν hence divides Σμ_e: M_G = gcd(Σμ_e, (r+l)ν+1) | Σμ_e ≤ ΣM_{H_e} (St 8.4). All-μ=1 IIa: d | (r+l)ν+1 ⇒ gcd(d,ν) = 1 ⇒ (d | rν ⇔ d | r), and (r+l)ν+1 ≡ lν+1 (mod d): **gcd(rν,(r+l)ν+1) = gcd(r, lν+1)** exactly (A1's "divides" upgraded to A2/A3's equality; elementary both ways). ZCH: dp = (r−1)ν+1, difference lν, coprimality to ν gives M = gcd((r−1)ν+1, l). ν = 1: q = p·s, M = gcd(r, r+l) = gcd(r,l). (Machine-swept: r ≤ 9, ν ≤ 12, l ≤ 12, mixed μ-vectors; reproduces every recorded engine cell — (2,3,1) → 2; ZCH (2,2,3) → 3; ν=1 (2,l=2) → 2.) (e) λ_G = 0 as in D5(e). ∎
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:4606:SIGRAY-AUDIT.md:54:| Prop 4.2 | 19 | GAP | NEW. All printed formulas re-derive exactly ((9), (10), δ-descent, uniqueness), but "since h_j is non-constant, l_j ≠ 0" conflates h_j with its leading part: if h⁺_{j,F} ∈ C* (finite nonzero asymptotic value — live for a non-proper Keller pair) the tower is stuck (l_j = 0 ∉ N*). The Remark "(7) automatic when d_F > 0" is circular. Repairs identified (constant-shift steps, or prove the (7)-analogue). Nil impact on all concrete campaign towers (nonconstant tops). Off-by-one N*^{m−1} tuple tags; stray ",b". |
