xmodel/sol-software2.md:45:The chart normalization is load-bearing. The global chart is `y = P(t) + eta*t^32`; ordinary `tf/tg` tails advance one `t`-level while the 21-ramified `tg01/tg02` series occupy only even global levels. Computing in `u = t^2` is allowed only with the explicit conversion `v_t = 2 v_u`. Multiplication by `W`, `A`, or a nonzero radical scalar is multiplication by a `t`-adic unit; multiplication or division by a power of `t` changes `e`. Also keep the uniformizer named `t` or `tau` distinct from the unrelated convention `t = eta^nu` elsewhere in the repository.
